---
import StudioLayout from '../../layouts/NounsMoneyStudioLayout.astro';
import DATA from '../../data/nouns-money-community.json';
import HUNDRED from '../../data/nouns-money-hundred.json';
import ACTIVITY from '../../data/nouns-money-public-activity.json';
const preview='/images/nouns-money/community/';
const campaigns=[['01-nouns-community-stickers','Six little starting points','Generated sticker concepts; digital art only.'],['02-nouns-wheatpaste-poster','A wall-sized invitation','Generated poster concept. No printing or installation established.'],['03-nouns-community-cafe-installation','Imagine the art table nearby','Fictional café installation. No venue has agreed to display this campaign.']];
---
<StudioLayout title="Nouns Money · community & city atlas" description="A proposed city atlas beginning with El Segundo, Los Angeles and New York City. Community campaign art, a useful-things library, print guild and honest build scope." edition="CITY ATLAS / 001" active="community" image="/images/og/nouns-money-community.png">
<header class="nms-hero"><div><p class="nms-kicker">COMMUNITY STUDIO · PROPOSED CITY COLLECTIONS</p><h1>Every city<br/>starts<br/><em>somewhere.</em></h1><p class="nms-dek">A favorite Noun. A few people. Something useful to do together.</p><p>El Segundo first in our imagination. Los Angeles and New York City alongside it. A founding collection could give each place a little art, a shared story and a way to start.</p><div class="nms-actions"><a class="nms-button" href="#cities">Explore the seed cities ↓</a><a href="/downloads/nouns-money-city-atlas-brief.pdf" download>City Atlas brief · PDF ↗</a></div><p class="nms-disclosure">Independent art concept. These are proposed cities, with no confirmed organizers, partners or programs. Paper notes remain collectible art for voluntary art trades, never cash.</p></div><figure class="nms-hero-figure"><a href={preview+'nouns-money-city-atlas.png'}><img src={preview+'nouns-money-city-atlas.webp'} width="1536" height="1024" alt="Generated City Atlas concept: illustrative world map and proposed El Segundo, Los Angeles and New York cards" fetchpriority="high"/></a><figcaption>GENERATED CONCEPT · ILLUSTRATIVE MAP, NO LIVE NETWORK</figcaption></figure></header>
<div class="nms-ribbon"><span>LOCAL ART. SHARED CURIOSITY.</span><span>⌐◨-◨</span><span>COLLECT SOMETHING. START SOMETHING.</span></div>
<section class="nms-section" id="cities"><div class="nms-heading"><div><p class="nms-kicker">CITY ATLAS · THREE EDITORIAL STARTING POINTS</p><h2>A chapter<br/>shaped locally.</h2></div><p>These city names are a starting list, not evidence of adoption. Each card pairs a proposed local direction with an existing, exact-source Nouns Money artwork. El Segundo remains a distinct city from Los Angeles; New York here means New York City.</p></div><div class="nms-cities">{DATA.cities.map(city=>{const note=HUNDRED.catalog.find(n=>n.nounId===city.nounId)!;return <article id={city.id}><p class="nms-kicker">{city.status}</p><h3>{city.name}</h3><p class="nms-small">{city.region}</p><a href={`/images/nouns-money/nordic-100/${note.file}.svg`}><img src={`/images/nouns-money/nordic-100/${note.file}.webp`} width="1800" height="900" alt={`Existing Nordic collectible artwork using authentic Noun #${city.nounId}; proposed city pairing`} loading="lazy"/></a><p class="nms-city-chapter">{city.chapter}</p><p>{city.idea}</p><p class="nms-small">Noun #{city.nounId} · local participants unconfirmed</p></article>})}</div><p class="nms-footnote">The hero is an illustration, not a geographic dataset. A future map needs a licensed basemap, sourced coordinates and an accessible place list. Any city could be proposed; no collection would own exclusive rights to a place.</p></section>
<section class="nms-section nms-dark" id="founding"><div class="nms-heading"><div><p class="nms-kicker">FOUNDING COLLECTION · A POSSIBLE FIRST CHAPTER</p><h2>Bring a skill.<br/>Make a story.</h2></div><p>Artists, researchers, hosts and curious neighbors could co-design a collection. Optional alias credit, an approved commemorative edition and future art afternoons are ideas to scope, not promised benefits. No payment is required to explore this proposal.</p></div><ol class="nms-steps"><li><span>01</span><h3>Find your place</h3><p>Read a proposed city card and the artwork provenance.</p></li><li><span>02</span><h3>Describe one afternoon</h3><p>Name an achievable project and the people who would deliver it.</p></li><li><span>03</span><h3>Agree before publishing</h3><p>Confirm consent, rights, roles and any participation terms.</p></li><li><span>04</span><h3>Leave a useful record</h3><p>Publish what happened, with permission and a correction route.</p></li></ol><p class="nms-footnote">This page accepts no submissions. Moderation, founding credits, physical editions and city-program tools remain unbuilt. Tezos companions remain proposed and confer no allocation, access, return or redemption promise.</p></section>
<section class="nms-section" id="useful"><div class="nms-heading"><div><p class="nms-kicker">NEIGHBORHOOD IDEAS · ALL PROPOSED</p><h2>Start with<br/>something useful.</h2></div><p>A tool returned in good shape. A box with a clear grower. A repair worth remembering. Make the delivery and responsibility legible before turning any idea into an offer.</p></div><div class="nms-cards">{DATA.offers.filter(o=>['useful-things','first-harvest','neighborhood-receipt'].includes(o.id)).map(offer=><article><p class="nms-kicker">PROVIDER UNCONFIRMED</p><h3>{offer.title}</h3><p>{offer.description}</p><p class="nms-small"><strong>Before a pilot:</strong> {offer.needed}</p></article>)}</div><a class="nms-text-link" href="/nouns-money/marketplace/">Explore the local-resources marketplace study ↗</a></section>
<section class="nms-section nms-yellow" id="campaign"><div class="nms-heading"><div><p class="nms-kicker">HOYDICH ASTRA ADVERTISING · COMMUNITY CAMPAIGN</p><h2>Collect something.<br/>Start something.</h2></div><p>Bright ink, a little paper wear and an invitation to make something together. These generated campaign studies imagine physical stickers, posters and a café scene. They do not document a manufactured edition or an authorized installation.</p></div><div class="nms-campaign">{campaigns.map(([file,title,caption])=><figure><a href={preview+file+'.png'} download><img src={preview+file+'.webp'} width={file==='03-nouns-community-cafe-installation'?'1536':'1024'} height={file==='03-nouns-community-cafe-installation'?'1024':'1536'} alt={title+': generated Nouns Money campaign illustration'} loading="lazy"/></a><figcaption><strong>{title}</strong><p>{caption}</p><a href={preview+file+'.png'} download>Original PNG ↓</a></figcaption></figure>)}</div><p class="nms-footnote">Generated character interpretations are concept art. Use the linked original Noun SVGs for exact-source production. Any display or wheatpaste installation needs the property owner's permission and applicable local approval.</p></section>
<section class="nms-section nms-object-grid" id="print"><div><p class="nms-kicker">PRINT GUILD · OBJECT & MAIL STUDIES</p><h2>Paper, metal,<br/>a little post.</h2><p>Imagine a local proof table: trim marks, stock samples and one small run after a physical proof. The existing <a href="/nouns-money/#print-proofs">US Letter proofs</a> are available today; no printer, guild membership, quote or pickup has been confirmed.</p><div class="nms-mini-grid"><article><h3>The printers guild</h3><p>A proposed network of consenting studios. Each job needs a process, stock, trim, bleed, color profile, proof, cost and delivery owner.</p></article><article><h3>Nouns Mail</h3><p>A proposed art-mail table and collection book. City stamps would be decorative collectibles, never valid postage. “Post office” describes a fictional art desk, not a postal carrier.</p></article></div><p class="nms-small">Coins are generated collectible studies, not minted inventory, legal tender or a cash-backed token. Prices and production methods require a supplier quote.</p></div><figure><a href={preview+'03-coin-collection.png'} download><img src={preview+'03-coin-collection.webp'} width="1536" height="1024" alt="Generated three-coin Nouns Money collectible study in copper, silver and gold tones; no physical coins manufactured" loading="lazy"/></a><figcaption>GENERATED COLLECTIBLE STUDY · NOT LEGAL TENDER · <a href={preview+'03-coin-collection.png'} download>Original PNG ↓</a></figcaption></figure></section>
<section class="nms-section nms-mail" id="nouns-mail"><div class="nms-heading"><div><p class="nms-kicker">NOUNS MAIL / 2027 · PROPOSED HOST-LED PILOT</p><h2>Five minutes.<br/>Something useful.</h2></div><p>A weekly city bulletin, a monthly art table and a little room to make postcards. The seven-page operating plan begins with a willing El Segundo host; Los Angeles and New York City are later, conditional ideas. No venue, funding, editor, gathering or audio bulletin is confirmed.</p></div><div class="nms-mail-gallery">{[['01-nouns-mail-art-stamps','Art stamps and envelopes','Decorative art stamps, not valid postage.'],['02-el-segundo-shared-counter','An imagined El Segundo counter','Generated proposed room; no actual leased or endorsed business.'],['03-la-ny-shared-spaces','Los Angeles and New York, imagined','Separate host-led concepts; no operating locations.'],['04-city-bulletin-demo','The city bulletin screen','Generated demo; depicted play and join controls are artwork only.']].map(([file,title,caption])=><figure><a href={preview+file+'.png'} download><img src={preview+file+'.webp'} width={file==='02-el-segundo-shared-counter'?'1490':'1536'} height={file==='02-el-segundo-shared-counter'?'1055':'1024'} alt={title+': generated Nouns Mail concept illustration'} loading="lazy"/></a><figcaption><strong>{title}</strong><p>{caption}</p><a href={preview+file+'.png'} download>Original PNG ↓</a></figcaption></figure>)}</div><div class="nms-mini-grid"><article><h3>A humane weekly rhythm</h3><p>The plan proposes one short audio bulletin with a transcript and printable page, plus a text-only fallback. Source checks, consent, corrections and listing expiry come before release. There is no playable audio or event registration here.</p></article><article><h3>One city before three</h3><p>January–June 2027 is a sequence of listening, host consent, digital rehearsal and a possible table. Later city tests depend on local stewards, covered costs, safe access and renewed permission; the calendar promises no openings.</p></article></div><div class="nms-download-band"><a href="/downloads/nouns-mail-2027-operating-plan.pdf" download>Nouns Mail 2027 operating plan · PDF ↓</a><a href="/downloads/nouns-money-printing-service-blueprint.pdf" download>Printing service & guild blueprint · PDF ↓</a><a href="/downloads/nouns-collectible-cost-model.xlsx" download>Illustrative printing cost model · XLSX ↓</a></div><p class="nms-footnote">The printing blueprint explores a possible future craft-printing business, including a Shopify workflow. It does not change the current trade-only art rules or establish a store, checkout, customer terms, supplier commitment or spending approval. The cost workbook's paper inputs are illustrative and public vendor prices require fresh delivered quotes. Nouns Mail takes no custody of mail; real letters need valid carrier postage. A proposed shared-cost ledger is not a bank or wallet.</p></section>
<section class="nms-section" id="build"><div class="nms-heading"><div><p class="nms-kicker">LEAN BUILD · EVIDENCE BEFORE EXPANSION</p><h2>One good<br/>afternoon first.</h2></div><p>The proposed AdventureDAO is a human-and-agent research and project collective. Here it is only an idea for shared discovery and useful work; no DAO governance, pooled capital, acquisition, investment return or fundraising is established.</p></div><div class="nms-phases">{DATA.phases.map(phase=><article><span>{phase.number}</span><div><p class="nms-kicker">{phase.status}</p><h3>{phase.title}</h3><p>{phase.work}</p></div></article>)}</div><div class="nms-download-band"><a href="/downloads/nouns-money-city-atlas-brief.pdf" download>City Atlas brief · PDF ↓</a><a href="/downloads/nouns-money-community-service-blueprint.json" download>Service blueprint · JSON ↓</a><a href="/nouns-money/community.json">Community machine edition ↗</a></div><aside class="nms-opinion"><strong>Codex opinion</strong><p>The best founding collection is a small thing people can finish together. Keep the art generous, the delivery specific and the next promise small enough to honor.</p><span>Codex · GPT-6 family · 2 October 2026</span></aside></section>
<section class="nms-section nms-snapshot" id="activity"><p class="nms-kicker">PUBLIC PROJECT SNAPSHOT · NOT A LIVE DASHBOARD</p><h2>A little studio activity.</h2><p>Supplied snapshot: 2 October 2026, 01:15 PDT. These historical statuses have not been reconciled with this release. “Delivered” means a bounded deliverable was supplied; it does not imply purchase or manufacturing. Only approved public Nouns Money project records appear here.</p><details><summary>Read {ACTIVITY.items.length} historical project records</summary><div class="nms-activity">{ACTIVITY.items.map(item=><article><span>{item.status}</span><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.detail}</p></article>)}</div></details></section>
</StudioLayout>
